# Python bytecode, which is not a suite artefact and was committed by accident.
#
# `run.sh --check` used to lint the two Python files with `python -m compileall`, which **writes**
# `__pycache__` beside them; two of those `.pyc` files were then swept into a commit whose subject
# was about something else entirely. They are removed here and `--check` no longer writes any — see
# the comment on that step. This line is the second half of that fix, because the first half only
# stops one of the ways they can appear: running `arms/textual/arm.py` at all creates them.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
